# The gate layer is executed by `sh` on every platform, including this repo's
# Windows checkouts. With the default core.autocrlf on Windows these files come
# back out of git with CRLF endings and sh fails on the carriage return
# (`$'\r': command not found`) — so the gate would break on a fresh clone of the
# very commit that added it. Pin them to LF.
*.sh text eol=lf
.githooks/* text eol=lf
